  "scope": "Scope-safe tombstone and purge, canonical export, authenticated encrypted backup, separately staged migration and restore, atomic activation, server-owned credentials and effects, and durable native authority/CLI recovery.",
  "source_adjustments": [
    "The declared deletion.rs behavior is implemented by the authoritative memory record operations plus lifecycle_security tombstone, derivative cleanup, retention and resurrection guards.",
    "The declared export.rs behavior is the canonical hypermid-memory export/import stream and Python portability contract; hypermid-store owns whole-SQLite recovery snapshots.",
    "Encrypted security backup is a canonical MemoryExportBundle JSONL artifact; lifecycle.export remains a distinct daemon-local recovery snapshot.",
    "The native security surface is SecurityRecovery rather than the earlier DataLifecycle placeholder path.",
    "Lifecycle recovery snapshots securely remove local credential-bound capability rows and bytes from the copied image before validation and manifest hashing.",
    "Daemon startup re-enrolls only the currently configured local operator grant after an authority-free restore."
  ]
